From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:56:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: skip graphics pipeline rebinds that would change
 nothing

DXVK 1.10 calls vkCmdBindPipeline whenever its pipeline state is dirty,
without comparing the handle, so many binds rebind the pipeline already
bound. vk_graphics_pipeline_cmd_bind() then walks every stage and
vk_dynamic_graphics_state_copy() compares every static state of the
pipeline against the command buffer's (about 100 branches): with
vk_graphics_pipeline_cmd_bind, 7.4% of PanVK's CPU samples in the Arkham
profile, for binds that change nothing.

vkCmdBindPipeline(GRAPHICS) now goes through a per-arch CmdBindPipeline.
It returns without binding when the pipeline is the one its last real
bind bound, every graphics shader pointer and the runtime's graphics
pipeline stage mask are still what that bind left, and no state the
pipeline has as static changed value since. Then the bind would change
nothing: the shader bind would compare equal pointers and the copy equal
values, so neither dirty bits nor any value differ from a real bind.

"Changed value since" comes from a new runtime bitset,
vk_dynamic_graphics_state::written, set next to dirty wherever the
runtime records a value change (SET_DYN_VALUE/ARRAY, the copy's
newly-set states, vkCmdSetVertexInputEXT) and never cleared by the
runtime. PanVK clears it after each real bind. Unlike dirty it isn't
cleared per draw, and a state already dirty still records a write, so it
covers vkCmdSet*() of a static state followed by a rebind, a pipeline
with that state dynamic bound in between (the handle differs) and
vk_meta (its pipeline bind replaces the last bound pipeline; its restore
copies the saved values and the matching written bits back). The static
state set comes from a new vk_graphics_pipeline_get_bind_state(); for
pipelines it returns NULL for, every bind runs. Reset and
vkCmdExecuteCommands zero the tracking with the rest of the graphics
state.

Compatibility channel. PANVK_NO_REBIND_SKIP=1 runs every bind again.

